.\" The manual page of the Linux packages (NP-055).
.TH KOONAPIN 1 "October 2026" "Koona Pin" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
koonapin \- desktop bookmark library
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B koonapin
.RB [ \-\-autostart ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Koona Pin keeps your bookmarks on your computer. Pages arrive from Chrome, Edge, Chromium and Firefox
with the button of the Koona Pin extension, also while the app is closed: the browser starts
.BR koonapin-host (1),
which starts the app hidden.
.PP
Only one Koona Pin runs in a session: a second start shows the window of the first and exits.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-autostart
Start hidden, without the window; the start with the session uses it.
.TP
.B \-\-register\-host
Register the native messaging host of this copy in the browsers of the current user, for a copy
run from a build folder. The package registers it for every user.
.TP
.B \-\-unregister\-host
Remove what
.B \-\-register\-host
wrote for this copy.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/Koona/Pin
The library and its backups (by default
.IR ~/.local/share/Koona/Pin ).
Removing the package leaves them in place.
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/autostart/koonapin.desktop
The start with the session, turned on by the first start and off in the settings.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR koonapin-host (1)
.PP
https://koona.app/pin/
